\f2\i\fs22 Protect culturally significant landmarks
\f0\i0 , he scribbled and drew an emoji of a laughing face. Then he drew laughing tears down the laughing face.\
Old money had been funding such things since Hardy was a boy, barely old enough to tie his laces,  but old enough to attend meetings with his grandfather. The old man would even take his advice occasionally, much to the horror of other attendees. Mandating clown suits as office-wear was a highlight\'97how ol\'92 grandad praised him that night was unforgettable. Clown Week became a celebrated block on the business calendar for years after.\
But back to 
\f2\i culturally significant landmarks. 
\f0\i0 Young Jamison learned the meaning of 
\f2\i euphemism 
\f0\i0 that same day, learning that 
\f2\i culture
\f0\i0 , 
\f2\i significance
\f0\i0 , and
\f2\i  landmark
\f0\i0  were all words that could be defined and owned by the boy with the most toys. Jamison liked the sound of that, and began to compile his own dictionary in a school exercise book with graph paper.\
